1
00:00:32,365 --> 00:00:39,372
‪FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

2
00:00:42,333 --> 00:00:45,253
‪Please stop anyone
‪who approaches the stage.

3
00:00:45,336 --> 00:00:47,297
‪-I'll do that.
‪-Thank you.

4
00:00:53,344 --> 00:00:54,220
‪Pi-o.

5
00:00:55,430 --> 00:00:57,807
‪Just one more time. Please?

6
00:00:58,850 --> 00:01:00,310
‪Think this over one more time.

7
00:01:01,478 --> 00:01:02,812
‪Once you go in,

8
00:01:03,688 --> 00:01:05,023
‪there's no turning back.

9
00:01:06,524 --> 00:01:08,193
‪I gave this a lot of thought.

10
00:01:09,152 --> 00:01:09,986
‪Thank you.

11
00:01:42,936 --> 00:01:44,270
‪My mother isn't the only one

12
00:01:45,480 --> 00:01:47,565
‪to blame for the abduction.

13
00:01:49,234 --> 00:01:50,151
‪I'm the one who used

14
00:01:51,319 --> 00:01:53,446
‪Conductor Choi Jeong-yo's sheet music

15
00:01:53,530 --> 00:01:55,698
‪to win the competition.

16
00:01:57,242 --> 00:01:58,076
‪Therefore,

17
00:01:59,202 --> 00:02:02,372
‪this entire incident happened
‪because of my own greed.

18
00:02:02,455 --> 00:02:07,877
‪Once again, I sincerely apologize
‪to Conductor Choi Jeong-yo…

19
00:02:10,338 --> 00:02:12,173
‪for the harm my mother and I caused.

20
00:02:14,134 --> 00:02:15,510
‪Therefore, as of today,

21
00:02:17,262 --> 00:02:18,972
‪I'm walking away from everything…

22
00:02:21,141 --> 00:02:22,392
‪I've been given.

23
00:02:23,726 --> 00:02:26,354
‪To everyone who has supported me…

24
00:02:28,398 --> 00:02:29,357
‪once again,

25
00:02:30,942 --> 00:02:32,610
‪I deeply apologize.

26
00:02:46,499 --> 00:02:48,877
‪What did you mean by winning
‪with his sheet music?

27
00:02:49,502 --> 00:02:51,588
‪Did you mean
‪you stole first place from him?

28
00:02:52,130 --> 00:02:54,465
‪Were you aware of your mother's crime?

29
00:02:54,549 --> 00:02:56,551
‪How long had you known about this?

30
00:02:56,634 --> 00:02:59,596
‪-Please elaborate.
‪-Please provide more specifics.

31
00:03:38,384 --> 00:03:40,178
‪FINALE

32
00:04:05,370 --> 00:04:07,080
‪HANKOOK SYMPHONY ANNOUNCEMENT CHAT

33
00:04:07,163 --> 00:04:11,000
‪REHEARSAL HAS BEEN POSTPONED
‪DUE TO MAESTRO KANG'S EMERGENCY SURGERY.

34
00:04:16,631 --> 00:04:18,883
‪SURGERY STATUS
‪KANG SEUNG-****: IN PROGRESS

35
00:04:27,225 --> 00:04:29,227
‪How did the surgery go?

36
00:04:29,310 --> 00:04:31,020
‪We did everything we could,

37
00:04:31,521 --> 00:04:34,524
‪but his heart was
‪already severely weakened.

38
00:04:35,358 --> 00:04:38,027
‪I'm sorry, but you should
‪prepare for the worst.

39
00:04:40,154 --> 00:04:40,989
‪How?

40
00:04:42,407 --> 00:04:44,701
‪How could this happen?

41
00:05:00,133 --> 00:05:01,009
‪Mr. Kang.

42
00:05:02,302 --> 00:05:04,012
‪I'm right here.

43
00:05:05,221 --> 00:05:06,055
‪Mr. Kang?

44
00:05:09,434 --> 00:05:12,103
‪Can you hear me?

45
00:05:13,062 --> 00:05:13,980
‪Why…

46
00:05:15,857 --> 00:05:18,026
‪Why didn't you tell me?

47
00:05:19,027 --> 00:05:20,361
‪Why did you keep it from me

48
00:05:21,112 --> 00:05:24,073
‪until things got so out of hand?

49
00:05:30,538 --> 00:05:31,372
‪What?

50
00:05:33,958 --> 00:05:35,668
‪Pi-o…

51
00:05:43,634 --> 00:05:44,469
‪Pi-o.

52
00:05:46,429 --> 00:05:48,681
‪Mr. Kang just woke up from anesthesia.

53
00:05:49,515 --> 00:05:50,558
‪He's asking for you.

54
00:05:52,268 --> 00:05:55,146
‪But he wants to see
‪you and Jeong-yo together.

55
00:05:55,730 --> 00:05:57,273
‪I think it's best if you call him.

56
00:06:23,883 --> 00:06:24,717
‪Hello?

57
00:06:26,135 --> 00:06:27,053
‪Where are you?

58
00:06:29,430 --> 00:06:30,681
‪How's Mr. Kang?

59
00:06:30,765 --> 00:06:32,266
‪He's out of surgery…

60
00:06:34,602 --> 00:06:35,895
‪and woke up from anesthesia.

61
00:06:35,978 --> 00:06:37,563
‪Then he's okay, right?

62
00:06:38,064 --> 00:06:38,981
<i>‪No.</i>

63
00:06:39,774 --> 00:06:40,858
‪The doctor said…

64
00:06:43,236 --> 00:06:44,612
‪we should prepare for the worst.

65
00:06:46,906 --> 00:06:49,158
‪He wants to see you one last time.

66
00:06:50,827 --> 00:06:52,036
‪Can you come?

67
00:07:37,665 --> 00:07:38,499
‪Mr. Kang.

68
00:07:39,459 --> 00:07:40,668
‪Mr. Kang?

69
00:07:41,252 --> 00:07:42,420
‪They're here.

70
00:07:55,057 --> 00:07:56,559
‪Go on in, Jeong-yo.

71
00:07:59,812 --> 00:08:01,105
‪Grandfather.

72
00:08:12,074 --> 00:08:13,159
‪I'm sorry.

73
00:08:15,870 --> 00:08:16,787
‪It's my fault.

74
00:08:18,247 --> 00:08:19,248
‪No.

75
00:08:21,584 --> 00:08:23,085
‪It's not your fault.

76
00:08:24,545 --> 00:08:26,547
‪It's just my time to go.

77
00:08:28,883 --> 00:08:30,760
‪Why are you sorry for that?

78
00:08:35,640 --> 00:08:37,141
‪So the two of you…

79
00:08:39,435 --> 00:08:42,146
‪have finally completed <i>‪Nemesis</i>‪.

80
00:08:42,230 --> 00:08:43,856
‪You did it.

81
00:08:46,984 --> 00:08:47,860
‪Pi-o.

82
00:08:52,281 --> 00:08:55,535
‪I thought you'd spend your whole life
‪chasing after Jeong-yo,

83
00:08:55,618 --> 00:08:57,787
‪only to torment yourself.

84
00:08:58,996 --> 00:09:01,207
‪That living in someone's shadow…

85
00:09:02,375 --> 00:09:05,127
‪would slowly eat you alive.

86
00:09:06,170 --> 00:09:07,046
‪But…

87
00:09:09,048 --> 00:09:10,383
‪Now I realize…

88
00:09:11,842 --> 00:09:13,261
‪that I was the one…

89
00:09:15,888 --> 00:09:16,889
‪who held you back.

90
00:09:18,474 --> 00:09:20,351
‪I let my pride get the better of me…

91
00:09:22,603 --> 00:09:25,690
‪and put you through hell

92
00:09:25,773 --> 00:09:27,358
‪when you were so young.

93
00:09:28,693 --> 00:09:30,278
‪Please forgive me.

94
00:09:48,421 --> 00:09:49,797
‪I'm sorry, Jeong-yo.

95
00:09:50,590 --> 00:09:53,551
‪I apologize on my daughter's behalf.

96
00:09:54,719 --> 00:09:56,554
‪The way she turned out…

97
00:10:00,182 --> 00:10:01,726
‪is all my fault.

98
00:10:03,311 --> 00:10:06,188
‪My cowardly actions caught up with me…

99
00:10:08,357 --> 00:10:10,526
‪and you had to suffer for it.

100
00:10:11,986 --> 00:10:13,029
‪I'm sorry.

101
00:10:15,781 --> 00:10:17,074
‪I'm sorry.

102
00:10:18,117 --> 00:10:19,201
‪All of this…

103
00:10:21,120 --> 00:10:22,246
‪is my fault.

104
00:10:24,373 --> 00:10:26,125
‪So will you please…

105
00:10:29,962 --> 00:10:31,922
‪forgive my foolish child?

106
00:11:08,626 --> 00:11:09,502
‪Pi-o.

107
00:11:13,130 --> 00:11:14,048
‪You must've resented

108
00:11:15,424 --> 00:11:17,218
‪your grandfather all this time.

109
00:11:21,180 --> 00:11:22,098
‪Still,

110
00:11:24,016 --> 00:11:26,352
‪I hope you won't
‪hold too much against him.

111
00:11:29,647 --> 00:11:31,190
‪One time…

112
00:11:32,983 --> 00:11:35,694
‪I asked your grandfather

113
00:11:36,362 --> 00:11:38,155
‪why he was so harsh to you.

114
00:11:40,032 --> 00:11:41,242
‪And he said

115
00:11:42,451 --> 00:11:43,411
‪it was because

116
00:11:44,620 --> 00:11:46,247
‪you take after him.

117
00:11:48,874 --> 00:11:50,918
‪That you push yourself to the limit…

118
00:11:52,962 --> 00:11:55,923
‪then choose to self-destruct
‪if it doesn't work out.

119
00:11:56,006 --> 00:11:58,801
‪He said you were just like him
‪in that regard.

120
00:12:00,761 --> 00:12:02,012
‪I think

121
00:12:03,055 --> 00:12:05,599
‪he may have felt tormented

122
00:12:06,559 --> 00:12:08,519
‪because your pain

123
00:12:09,186 --> 00:12:11,689
‪was just too clear to him.

124
00:12:17,027 --> 00:12:18,070
‪Excuse me, ma'am.

125
00:12:18,863 --> 00:12:20,865
‪We have a few things to go over.

126
00:12:39,091 --> 00:12:40,050
<i>‪Well,</i>

127
00:12:40,634 --> 00:12:41,927
‪today wasn't half bad.

128
00:12:43,471 --> 00:12:45,681
‪Invite me to your next performance.

129
00:12:52,521 --> 00:12:53,856
‪Grandfather.

130
00:12:56,275 --> 00:12:57,985
‪Break the mold, Pi-o.

131
00:12:58,652 --> 00:13:01,155
‪Stop relying on that chunk of metal,

132
00:13:01,238 --> 00:13:03,949
‪and find your own inner rhythm.

133
00:13:18,380 --> 00:13:19,715
‪Pi-o.

134
00:13:20,299 --> 00:13:22,384
‪Yes, Grandfather?

135
00:13:26,180 --> 00:13:30,643
‪I want to hear your rendition
‪of the <i>‪Moonlight Sonata.</i>

136
00:13:58,045 --> 00:13:59,255
‪How nice.

137
00:14:00,673 --> 00:14:01,549
‪Grandfather.

138
00:14:02,716 --> 00:14:03,968
‪When you get better,

139
00:14:04,051 --> 00:14:06,804
‪I'll play you a version
‪that's even better than this.

140
00:14:07,972 --> 00:14:09,139
‪You see,

141
00:14:09,223 --> 00:14:11,725
‪I think I can play from the heart now.

142
00:14:18,941 --> 00:14:20,150
‪Let me be alone…

143
00:14:22,653 --> 00:14:25,239
‪with the music for a moment.

144
00:14:30,119 --> 00:14:31,036
‪Okay.

145
00:15:37,353 --> 00:15:38,562
‪Grandfather?

146
00:15:43,067 --> 00:15:44,068
‪Grandfather.

147
00:15:44,151 --> 00:15:45,277
‪Grandfather.

148
00:15:46,570 --> 00:15:48,113
‪Grandfather!

149
00:16:13,389 --> 00:16:15,599
<i>‪In accordance with our custom,</i>

150
00:16:15,683 --> 00:16:18,185
<i>‪we now commit this body to the ground.</i>

151
00:16:19,436 --> 00:16:24,984
<i>‪Lord, grant eternal rest to our brother,</i>
<i>‪Kang Seung-woon John.</i>

152
00:16:25,693 --> 00:16:29,196
<i>‪-May perpetual light shine upon him.</i>
<i>‪-May perpetual light shine upon him.</i>

153
00:16:29,947 --> 00:16:34,243
<i>‪Receive his soul and present him</i>

154
00:16:34,326 --> 00:16:35,619
<i>‪to God the Most High.</i>

155
00:16:36,161 --> 00:16:38,122
<i>‪Most merciful Father,</i>

156
00:16:38,205 --> 00:16:42,751
<i>‪we are filled with the sure hope</i>
<i>‪that our departed will rise again…</i>

157
00:16:48,340 --> 00:16:50,759
‪THE LATE KANG SEUNG-WOON JOHN
‪FUNERAL MASS

158
00:16:50,843 --> 00:16:52,553
<i>‪Father…</i>

159
00:16:54,555 --> 00:16:56,348
<i>‪This is all your fault, Father.</i>

160
00:16:57,516 --> 00:17:01,270
‪If you had been kind to Pi-o,
‪I wouldn't have done it.

161
00:17:02,730 --> 00:17:04,898
‪If only you had acknowledged him,

162
00:17:04,982 --> 00:17:07,234
‪I wouldn't have done something this crazy!

163
00:17:07,317 --> 00:17:08,694
‪How could you do that?

164
00:17:08,777 --> 00:17:10,195
‪How could you do that to me?

165
00:17:10,279 --> 00:17:11,488
‪How could you do that to Pi-o?

166
00:17:11,572 --> 00:17:12,906
‪Explain yourself!

167
00:17:12,990 --> 00:17:16,410
‪How could you do that?

168
00:17:20,164 --> 00:17:21,957
‪How could you?

169
00:17:22,041 --> 00:17:25,502
‪How could you do that, Father?

170
00:17:35,387 --> 00:17:37,264
‪OPENING THE FUTURE
‪THROUGH ORDER AND HUMAN RIGHTS

171
00:17:37,347 --> 00:17:40,309
<i>‪Ms. Kang has refused to receive visitors.</i>

172
00:18:04,500 --> 00:18:08,545
‪KANG PI-O

173
00:18:49,169 --> 00:18:51,713
‪Do you really have to do this?

174
00:19:03,559 --> 00:19:04,476
‪I get it.

175
00:19:04,560 --> 00:19:06,603
‪I know you're heartbroken.

176
00:19:06,687 --> 00:19:09,231
‪-But saying you'll never play--
‪-Please stop.

177
00:19:10,899 --> 00:19:12,484
‪I'll never play again.

178
00:19:14,528 --> 00:19:15,821
‪All of this happened

179
00:19:15,904 --> 00:19:18,407
‪because of my greed.

180
00:19:20,450 --> 00:19:21,493
<i>‪His piano is up for sale.</i>

181
00:19:21,577 --> 00:19:23,328
‪-Hello.
‪-Are you serious?

182
00:19:24,204 --> 00:19:26,623
‪Kang Pi-o's piano is up for sale?

183
00:19:26,707 --> 00:19:29,877
‪Yeah. Looks like he's really quitting.

184
00:19:29,960 --> 00:19:32,337
‪Jeez, that idiot.

185
00:19:32,421 --> 00:19:34,506
‪I thought he finally got his touch back.

186
00:19:34,590 --> 00:19:36,008
‪Then again,

187
00:19:36,091 --> 00:19:38,343
‪if he thinks Maestro Kang died
‪because of him,

188
00:19:38,427 --> 00:19:40,846
‪how could he bring himself to play again?

189
00:19:41,638 --> 00:19:42,848
‪I know, right?

190
00:19:43,390 --> 00:19:47,352
‪Who'd have known such a powerful family
‪would end up in ruins like this?

191
00:19:48,020 --> 00:19:49,980
‪Anyway, pianists everywhere

192
00:19:50,063 --> 00:19:53,066
‪are fighting over it,
‪even offering to pay a premium.

193
00:19:55,360 --> 00:19:56,820
‪Why is your phone turned off?

194
00:19:58,113 --> 00:19:59,031
‪Oh…

195
00:19:59,114 --> 00:20:00,407
‪You have a guest.

196
00:20:00,490 --> 00:20:02,326
‪He's been waiting all afternoon.

197
00:20:02,409 --> 00:20:05,954
‪I told him to return later,
‪but he insisted on waiting.

198
00:20:14,546 --> 00:20:15,589
‪What are you doing here?

199
00:20:16,215 --> 00:20:17,257
‪Take a seat.

200
00:20:26,183 --> 00:20:27,100
‪Why did you come?

201
00:20:27,184 --> 00:20:28,977
‪Why did you sell your piano?

202
00:20:30,520 --> 00:20:31,772
‪That's why you're here?

203
00:20:31,855 --> 00:20:32,814
‪Yeah.

204
00:20:35,275 --> 00:20:36,485
‪Because I don't need it anymore.

205
00:20:42,908 --> 00:20:46,078
‪I asked Mr. Kang something
‪before he passed away.

206
00:20:47,704 --> 00:20:50,874
‪I asked if he believed flawed artists
‪don't deserve to make art.

207
00:20:51,458 --> 00:20:52,834
‪Then he told me

208
00:20:53,710 --> 00:20:57,297
‪that if anything,
‪one must be flawed to make art.

209
00:21:00,634 --> 00:21:02,427
‪So keep playing the piano.

210
00:21:03,470 --> 00:21:04,930
‪All we can do is…

211
00:21:06,348 --> 00:21:08,183
‪just keep making music.

212
00:21:10,060 --> 00:21:11,520
‪Thanks for saying that.

213
00:21:12,104 --> 00:21:12,938
‪But…

214
00:21:14,022 --> 00:21:16,400
‪I can't forgive myself.

215
00:21:17,067 --> 00:21:19,278
‪It's because I insisted on pursuing music

216
00:21:19,361 --> 00:21:22,948
‪that my mom ended up the way she did
‪and my grandfather died.

217
00:21:25,993 --> 00:21:27,160
‪I'm responsible for your hand too.

218
00:21:59,151 --> 00:22:00,902
‪HYUN-CHUL

219
00:22:01,862 --> 00:22:02,779
‪Hello?

220
00:22:02,863 --> 00:22:04,156
<i>‪The hospital called.</i>

221
00:22:04,823 --> 00:22:06,158
<i>‪He wants to see you.</i>

222
00:22:08,035 --> 00:22:10,704
‪I guess he already knew you were back.

223
00:22:11,830 --> 00:22:12,998
‪He called a nurse over

224
00:22:13,081 --> 00:22:15,167
‪and told her he wanted to see you.

225
00:22:16,001 --> 00:22:19,629
‪I guess it'd be weird if he didn't know,
‪since you were all over the news.

226
00:22:23,967 --> 00:22:25,969
‪Our project is over now, right?

227
00:22:27,137 --> 00:22:28,388
‪Regardless of how it went down,

228
00:22:28,472 --> 00:22:30,348
‪they're paying for what they did.

229
00:22:32,142 --> 00:22:33,810
‪But why don't I feel relieved?

230
00:22:37,606 --> 00:22:39,024
‪You wanted to see me?

231
00:22:40,984 --> 00:22:42,778
‪When did you find out I returned?

232
00:22:43,779 --> 00:22:47,240
‪When you first got back to Korea.

233
00:22:47,824 --> 00:22:50,202
‪Then why are you only reaching out now?

234
00:22:53,997 --> 00:22:55,415
‪I felt like I had no right to.

235
00:23:01,546 --> 00:23:02,964
‪Here, have some.

236
00:23:03,048 --> 00:23:04,508
‪I know you like it.

237
00:23:05,842 --> 00:23:06,676
‪Why did you do it?

238
00:23:08,220 --> 00:23:10,847
‪You should've just let me die in a ditch.

239
00:23:12,808 --> 00:23:14,559
‪Why did you waste your money on me?

240
00:23:17,062 --> 00:23:19,523
‪Because you were good to me,
‪if only briefly.

241
00:23:21,233 --> 00:23:22,984
‪I know you want to forget,

242
00:23:23,735 --> 00:23:25,904
‪but you were good to me when I was young.

243
00:23:27,989 --> 00:23:29,574
‪And I wanted to repay you for that.

244
00:23:30,700 --> 00:23:31,535
‪Back then,

245
00:23:33,078 --> 00:23:34,287
‪I took my anger out on you.

246
00:23:35,497 --> 00:23:36,790
‪I'm sorry I did that.

247
00:23:38,041 --> 00:23:39,000
‪From now on…

248
00:23:40,627 --> 00:23:42,170
‪don't spend your money on me.

249
00:23:42,254 --> 00:23:44,172
‪I've got blood on my hands.

250
00:23:49,261 --> 00:23:50,637
‪I killed your mom.

251
00:23:52,347 --> 00:23:54,599
‪I raged about how she betrayed me,

252
00:23:55,600 --> 00:23:56,935
‪yet I refused to divorce her.

253
00:23:57,894 --> 00:24:00,313
‪I kept her close and tormented her

254
00:24:01,273 --> 00:24:02,816
‪until her last breath.

255
00:24:03,316 --> 00:24:04,317
‪In the end…

256
00:24:06,903 --> 00:24:09,114
‪I drained the life out of your mother.

257
00:24:10,532 --> 00:24:12,325
‪I expected to feel relief.

258
00:24:12,909 --> 00:24:15,912
‪But instead, it turns out…

259
00:24:17,914 --> 00:24:19,541
‪I just destroyed myself.

260
00:24:33,221 --> 00:24:34,806
<i>‪I expected to feel relief.</i>

261
00:24:35,515 --> 00:24:38,226
<i>‪But instead, it turns out…</i>

262
00:24:39,269 --> 00:24:40,896
<i>‪I just destroyed myself.</i>

263
00:24:43,899 --> 00:24:45,734
‪CHOI JEONG-YO

264
00:24:54,701 --> 00:24:55,660
‪What is it?

265
00:24:55,744 --> 00:24:56,786
<i>‪What are you doing?</i>

266
00:24:56,870 --> 00:24:58,246
‪Why are you calling?

267
00:24:58,830 --> 00:25:00,874
‪Come outside. I'm at your house.

268
00:25:12,427 --> 00:25:13,428
‪Why are you here again?

269
00:25:13,511 --> 00:25:16,306
‪Come with me.
‪I want to show you something.

270
00:25:31,947 --> 00:25:33,573
‪Why are we taking the bus?

271
00:25:34,824 --> 00:25:36,117
‪Just because.

272
00:25:36,201 --> 00:25:37,619
‪Brings back memories, right?

273
00:25:47,087 --> 00:25:47,921
‪Why are we here?

274
00:26:09,109 --> 00:26:10,110
‪What's this?

275
00:26:10,735 --> 00:26:13,113
‪What do you think? It's your piano.

276
00:26:13,697 --> 00:26:14,990
‪I bought it back.

277
00:26:15,073 --> 00:26:16,116
‪Yes, but why?

278
00:26:16,199 --> 00:26:18,702
‪Because you'll need it
‪when you play again.

279
00:26:19,703 --> 00:26:20,829
‪I said I'm done.

280
00:26:20,912 --> 00:26:22,831
‪You shouldn't have wasted your time.

281
00:26:29,379 --> 00:26:30,839
‪Sit down.

282
00:27:23,391 --> 00:27:24,517
‪What's going on?

283
00:27:25,101 --> 00:27:27,103
‪Why? You surprised?

284
00:27:27,812 --> 00:27:31,066
‪I kept up with my hospital treatments
‪just in case.

285
00:27:31,149 --> 00:27:34,110
‪Then somehow, my fingers started working.

286
00:27:35,987 --> 00:27:36,988
‪Well?

287
00:27:37,072 --> 00:27:38,365
‪Was it any good?

288
00:27:44,662 --> 00:27:45,914
‪Does this mean…

289
00:27:47,624 --> 00:27:49,209
‪you can play the piano again?

290
00:27:50,752 --> 00:27:51,586
‪Yeah.

291
00:27:55,256 --> 00:27:57,258
‪What's that look for?

292
00:27:59,344 --> 00:28:02,305
‪Now do you understand
‪why I dragged you all the way here?

293
00:28:03,932 --> 00:28:04,891
‪At the very least,

294
00:28:05,475 --> 00:28:08,144
‪I want you to stop
‪feeling guilty about me.

295
00:28:10,355 --> 00:28:11,856
‪And do me one last favor.

296
00:28:16,277 --> 00:28:17,445
‪Play the piano again.

297
00:28:22,283 --> 00:28:23,243
‪I thought about

298
00:28:24,244 --> 00:28:27,664
‪why I started playing the piano again
‪when I was young.

299
00:28:29,040 --> 00:28:31,501
<i>‪You just came out of nowhere</i>

300
00:28:31,584 --> 00:28:33,086
<i>‪and stormed into my miserable life.</i>

301
00:28:34,254 --> 00:28:35,713
‪You think playing the piano is a joke?

302
00:28:36,214 --> 00:28:40,427
<i>‪You made me ashamed</i>
<i>‪of how I refused to take music seriously.</i>

303
00:28:40,510 --> 00:28:42,303
<i>‪We practiced this hundreds of times.</i>

304
00:28:42,387 --> 00:28:44,514
<i>‪Ignore everyone else.</i>

305
00:28:44,597 --> 00:28:46,307
<i>‪Forget where we are.</i>

306
00:28:46,391 --> 00:28:49,018
<i>‪I was drowning in my trauma,</i>

307
00:28:49,102 --> 00:28:50,770
<i>‪but you pulled me out.</i>

308
00:28:51,396 --> 00:28:52,230
‪Play freely…

309
00:28:53,690 --> 00:28:54,774
‪like that day.

310
00:28:55,525 --> 00:28:57,026
‪Looking back,

311
00:28:58,486 --> 00:29:00,405
‪when I was lost in despair,

312
00:29:00,488 --> 00:29:03,283
<i>‪you were the one</i>
<i>‪who pulled me back into music.</i>

313
00:29:03,366 --> 00:29:05,535
<i>‪Whether you meant to be or not,</i>

314
00:29:06,411 --> 00:29:09,122
‪you were my light and hope.

315
00:29:11,207 --> 00:29:13,793
‪Even when I was consumed by revenge…

316
00:29:16,171 --> 00:29:19,632
‪I'd fall asleep dreaming of
‪playing four hands with you.

317
00:29:22,635 --> 00:29:24,846
‪Then I heard you were quitting the piano,

318
00:29:24,929 --> 00:29:26,139
‪so how do you think I felt?

319
00:29:27,682 --> 00:29:28,933
‪But…

320
00:29:30,101 --> 00:29:31,770
‪I stole your sheet music.

321
00:29:34,481 --> 00:29:36,232
‪And I stole your life.

322
00:29:36,316 --> 00:29:38,485
‪Man, you're so frustrating.

323
00:29:39,569 --> 00:29:40,904
‪Hey, Kang Pi-o.

324
00:29:42,405 --> 00:29:45,492
‪You interpreted that piece
‪and made it complete.

325
00:29:45,575 --> 00:29:46,785
‪The place you're at…

326
00:29:48,536 --> 00:29:50,163
‪was always yours.

327
00:29:51,998 --> 00:29:53,166
‪Neither of us can survive…

328
00:29:56,419 --> 00:29:59,255
‪unless we're immersed in music.

329
00:29:59,964 --> 00:30:03,343
‪We were born that way. Don't you get it?

330
00:30:07,597 --> 00:30:09,599
‪Remember Bach's Cantata No. 106?

331
00:30:14,145 --> 00:30:15,063
‪Get over here.

332
00:30:30,995 --> 00:30:31,996
‪All right.

333
00:30:32,622 --> 00:30:33,873
‪I'll play secondo.

334
00:30:34,707 --> 00:30:35,667
‪You play primo.

335
00:30:37,210 --> 00:30:38,253
‪Play freely…

336
00:30:39,796 --> 00:30:41,047
‪like that day.

337
00:32:28,071 --> 00:32:29,238
‪Thanks, Jeong-yo.

338
00:32:30,823 --> 00:32:31,908
‪You did it again.

339
00:32:33,785 --> 00:32:35,411
‪You pulled me out of my despair.

340
00:32:37,830 --> 00:32:38,873
‪No, I didn't.

341
00:32:40,291 --> 00:32:41,417
‪Didn't you hear what I said?

342
00:32:44,504 --> 00:32:46,172
‪It's really weird.

343
00:32:47,173 --> 00:32:48,466
‪We were at each other's throats,

344
00:32:48,549 --> 00:32:50,760
‪but whenever I was actually lost in music,

345
00:32:52,136 --> 00:32:53,346
‪you were always there.

346
00:32:54,806 --> 00:32:56,557
‪Ten years ago,

347
00:32:57,308 --> 00:32:59,268
‪when I said
‪I wouldn't enter any competitions

348
00:33:00,770 --> 00:33:04,107
‪and just wanted to be happy
‪making music with you…

349
00:33:06,651 --> 00:33:08,653
‪Looking back, that was the right call.

350
00:33:12,323 --> 00:33:13,449
‪It's not too late.

351
00:33:14,617 --> 00:33:16,119
‪Let's have fun making music.

352
00:33:20,373 --> 00:33:21,332
‪No way.

353
00:33:22,417 --> 00:33:26,212
‪I don't want to put up with
‪your same old prickly attitude.

354
00:33:27,463 --> 00:33:29,090
‪And the way I see it,

355
00:33:29,674 --> 00:33:31,801
‪you don't need my help anymore.

356
00:33:31,884 --> 00:33:34,429
‪Hey, just say no if you don't want to.

357
00:33:35,013 --> 00:33:36,431
‪You don't let things go, do you?

358
00:33:36,514 --> 00:33:37,640
‪Of course not.

359
00:33:38,516 --> 00:33:40,393
‪That's why I came after you.

360
00:33:45,314 --> 00:33:46,399
‪I had fun today.

361
00:33:48,067 --> 00:33:49,027
‪Thanks.

362
00:33:53,406 --> 00:33:55,199
‪Have a good night and rest well.

363
00:33:57,118 --> 00:33:58,369
‪See you around.

364
00:33:58,953 --> 00:33:59,871
‪Okay.

365
00:34:30,943 --> 00:34:31,819
‪Hello?

366
00:34:31,903 --> 00:34:33,196
<i>‪Pi-o.</i>

367
00:34:33,279 --> 00:34:35,740
<i>‪Have you spoken to Jeong-yo recently?</i>

368
00:34:36,574 --> 00:34:37,867
‪I saw him yesterday.

369
00:34:38,618 --> 00:34:39,786
‪Why?

370
00:34:39,869 --> 00:34:43,498
<i>‪Jeong-yo put in his resignation</i>
<i>‪and won't answer his phone.</i>

371
00:34:44,499 --> 00:34:46,542
<i>‪Did he say anything yesterday?</i>

372
00:34:51,464 --> 00:34:53,216
<i>‪The phone is turned off.</i>

373
00:34:53,299 --> 00:34:55,843
<i>‪You will be connected to voicemail</i>
<i>‪after the beep</i>‪…

374
00:34:57,804 --> 00:34:59,514
<i>‪I think he prepared ahead of time.</i>

375
00:35:00,223 --> 00:35:03,851
<i>‪He emailed not just me</i>
<i>‪but the admin office and staff too.</i>

376
00:35:04,352 --> 00:35:06,771
<i>‪Are you sure he didn't mention anything?</i>

377
00:35:09,148 --> 00:35:10,608
<i>‪The phone is turned off.</i>

378
00:35:10,691 --> 00:35:14,862
<i>‪You will be connected to voicemail</i>
<i>‪after the beep…</i>

379
00:35:40,471 --> 00:35:41,347
<i>‪Kang Pi-o.</i>

380
00:35:42,056 --> 00:35:43,558
<i>‪I knew you'd come.</i>

381
00:35:44,433 --> 00:35:46,394
<i>‪By the time you find this letter,</i>

382
00:35:47,019 --> 00:35:48,604
<i>‪I'll be gone.</i>

383
00:35:49,856 --> 00:35:50,815
<i>‪I'm sorry,</i>

384
00:35:51,691 --> 00:35:54,443
<i>‪but I can't do that last favor for you.</i>

385
00:35:57,488 --> 00:35:59,574
<i>‪Maybe what happened between us…</i>

386
00:36:01,909 --> 00:36:06,664
<i>‪came from our deep longing</i>
<i>‪and love for music.</i>

387
00:36:09,792 --> 00:36:12,253
<i>‪Even though it caused a lot of pain,</i>

388
00:36:12,336 --> 00:36:16,215
<i>‪seeing your passion for music</i>
<i>‪taught me a great deal.</i>

389
00:36:18,050 --> 00:36:19,135
<i>‪So now,</i>

390
00:36:19,927 --> 00:36:21,971
<i>‪I'm leaving to make music</i>
<i>‪that comforts others</i>

391
00:36:23,181 --> 00:36:26,517
<i>‪rather than music</i>
<i>‪filled with resentment and hate.</i>

392
00:36:27,393 --> 00:36:30,479
<i>‪My misunderstandings caused you pain,</i>

393
00:36:31,063 --> 00:36:33,774
<i>‪but maybe I was obsessed</i>
<i>‪with getting revenge</i>

394
00:36:35,151 --> 00:36:39,155
<i>‪simply because I missed the days</i>
<i>‪we used to play piano together.</i>

395
00:36:39,238 --> 00:36:42,158
‪MUSICAL INSTRUMENT ARCADE
‪TRADITIONAL MARKET

396
00:36:42,241 --> 00:36:43,492
<i>‪I'm sorry for everything.</i>

397
00:36:44,535 --> 00:36:45,494
<i>‪And thank you.</i>

398
00:36:46,871 --> 00:36:48,623
<i>‪Whatever you do, don't give up.</i>

399
00:36:48,706 --> 00:36:51,042
<i>‪I hope you become a great musician.</i>

400
00:37:14,815 --> 00:37:18,110
‪3 YEARS LATER

401
00:37:31,749 --> 00:37:32,750
‪Hey, Pi-o.

402
00:37:34,460 --> 00:37:36,212
‪Goodness, that looks amazing.

403
00:37:37,922 --> 00:37:40,216
‪You didn't have to come all this way
‪with your busy schedule.

404
00:37:40,299 --> 00:37:42,927
‪I kept saying I'd come, but I never did.

405
00:37:43,010 --> 00:37:45,388
‪So I was determined to come today.

406
00:37:47,056 --> 00:37:48,140
‪How's it coming along?

407
00:39:06,135 --> 00:39:07,970
‪How's running the agency?
‪Are you holding up?

408
00:39:08,763 --> 00:39:10,681
‪It's hard but fun.

409
00:39:10,765 --> 00:39:12,558
‪Now that I'm doing it myself,

410
00:39:12,641 --> 00:39:15,436
‪I totally understand
‪how hard it was for my mom.

411
00:39:16,228 --> 00:39:19,148
‪I have a whole new level
‪of respect for her now.

412
00:39:19,231 --> 00:39:21,108
‪Hyun-jeong is something else.

413
00:39:21,192 --> 00:39:23,819
‪How did she hand you the reins
‪and just walk away?

414
00:39:23,903 --> 00:39:25,154
‪Does she nag you?

415
00:39:25,905 --> 00:39:27,156
‪Not at all.

416
00:39:27,239 --> 00:39:30,451
‪But that stresses me out more, you know?

417
00:39:30,534 --> 00:39:32,078
‪I don't want to disappoint her.

418
00:39:33,579 --> 00:39:36,207
‪Jae-in, you're really becoming a grown-up.

419
00:39:37,875 --> 00:39:39,502
‪This is on the house.

420
00:39:41,003 --> 00:39:43,339
‪Just a little thank-you for the concert.

421
00:39:44,715 --> 00:39:45,800
‪Thank you.

422
00:39:46,425 --> 00:39:48,928
‪Call me anytime, and I'll come play.

423
00:39:49,011 --> 00:39:50,554
‪Really?

424
00:39:51,138 --> 00:39:53,557
‪Goodness, thank you. How wonderful.

425
00:39:53,641 --> 00:39:55,267
‪Please enjoy your meal.

426
00:39:55,851 --> 00:39:57,478
‪-Thank you.
‪-Thank you.

427
00:39:57,978 --> 00:40:00,773
‪As always, everyone loves you
‪wherever you go.

428
00:40:02,316 --> 00:40:04,652
‪-Go ask him.
‪-No, you do it.

429
00:40:05,236 --> 00:40:06,779
‪-Go ask.
‪-Hurry up and ask.

430
00:40:06,862 --> 00:40:08,823
‪-No, you ask him.
‪-No, you.

431
00:40:08,906 --> 00:40:10,199
‪Do you have something to ask?

432
00:40:11,992 --> 00:40:14,787
‪We watched your performance earlier.

433
00:40:15,454 --> 00:40:17,206
‪What's your name?

434
00:40:17,289 --> 00:40:19,250
‪You're famous, right?
‪Can we get an autograph?

435
00:40:21,627 --> 00:40:23,504
‪I'm not that famous.

436
00:40:30,010 --> 00:40:33,013
‪Still, I really liked your performance.

437
00:40:33,097 --> 00:40:34,098
‪Me too.

438
00:40:34,682 --> 00:40:35,599
‪Thanks.

439
00:40:36,225 --> 00:40:37,101
‪Enjoy your meal.

440
00:40:37,184 --> 00:40:38,185
‪-Thank you!
‪-Thank you!

441
00:40:38,978 --> 00:40:40,438
‪See? He's not famous.

442
00:40:40,521 --> 00:40:41,897
‪But my mom said that he is.

443
00:40:42,481 --> 00:40:44,733
‪Why didn't you tell them your name?

444
00:40:45,359 --> 00:40:46,360
‪Was it deliberate?

445
00:40:47,445 --> 00:40:48,362
‪I guess…

446
00:40:50,114 --> 00:40:52,450
‪I don't want to be remembered
‪by my name anymore.

447
00:41:02,585 --> 00:41:04,420
‪OPENING THE FUTURE
‪THROUGH ORDER AND HUMAN RIGHTS

448
00:41:04,503 --> 00:41:06,505
‪-Mom!
‪-Gosh, Yun-jeong!

449
00:41:07,631 --> 00:41:09,508
‪-I'm sorry, sweetheart.
‪-Good job hanging in there.

450
00:41:09,592 --> 00:41:10,468
‪Ji-hye.

451
00:41:53,552 --> 00:41:54,428
‪Seon-ju.

452
00:42:17,618 --> 00:42:20,621
‪LEAVING A PROFOUND IMPACT IN HIS WAKE
‪CONDUCTOR KANG SEUNG-WOON

453
00:42:37,263 --> 00:42:38,222
‪Father.

454
00:42:39,181 --> 00:42:41,100
‪THE LATE KANG SEUNG-WOON JOHN

455
00:42:44,270 --> 00:42:45,229
‪I'm here.

456
00:42:55,197 --> 00:42:56,282
‪Hyun-soo.

457
00:42:58,325 --> 00:42:59,535
‪Thank you for today.

458
00:43:01,370 --> 00:43:04,915
‪It weighed on me not being there
‪when my father passed,

459
00:43:05,916 --> 00:43:07,543
‪but some of that weight

460
00:43:08,210 --> 00:43:09,503
‪has finally been lifted.

461
00:43:10,254 --> 00:43:11,880
‪It must have been hard for you.

462
00:43:12,923 --> 00:43:13,799
‪No.

463
00:43:14,341 --> 00:43:15,676
‪I'm much better now.

464
00:43:17,052 --> 00:43:18,679
‪You don't have to worry about me anymore.

465
00:43:19,263 --> 00:43:20,472
‪From now on,

466
00:43:20,556 --> 00:43:23,142
‪don't waste your time on me.

467
00:43:23,225 --> 00:43:24,643
‪It makes me feel bad.

468
00:43:25,811 --> 00:43:26,687
‪I can't do that.

469
00:43:28,647 --> 00:43:31,317
‪If I want to become happy…

470
00:43:33,193 --> 00:43:34,820
‪I need you by my side.

471
00:43:36,488 --> 00:43:37,865
‪I have no right to.

472
00:43:47,249 --> 00:43:49,627
‪All I need is you, Ji-hye.

473
00:43:50,711 --> 00:43:51,962
‪We'll take it easy.

474
00:43:56,425 --> 00:43:57,384
‪Like friends.

475
00:44:17,363 --> 00:44:18,530
‪Sorry.

476
00:44:19,365 --> 00:44:20,616
‪Have you been waiting long?

477
00:44:21,617 --> 00:44:23,035
‪No, I just ordered.

478
00:44:23,535 --> 00:44:25,079
‪Hurry up and eat while it's warm.

479
00:44:25,996 --> 00:44:26,955
‪It's what you wanted.

480
00:44:27,831 --> 00:44:30,209
‪I've never seen
‪a chicken sandwich this big.

481
00:44:30,292 --> 00:44:33,420
‪I'm so obsessed with it
‪that I have it for lunch every day.

482
00:44:39,843 --> 00:44:40,678
‪It's so good.

483
00:44:41,845 --> 00:44:43,597
‪Hey, go ahead and try it.

484
00:44:43,681 --> 00:44:44,598
‪Okay.

485
00:44:51,438 --> 00:44:52,314
‪This is good.

486
00:44:55,192 --> 00:44:56,110
‪Oh, right.

487
00:45:02,991 --> 00:45:03,826
‪Jae-in.

488
00:45:05,077 --> 00:45:06,286
‪It's good that you're working,

489
00:45:06,954 --> 00:45:08,497
‪but aren't you overdoing it?

490
00:45:09,456 --> 00:45:10,416
‪Don't get me started.

491
00:45:11,125 --> 00:45:12,459
‪I was just heading out the door

492
00:45:12,543 --> 00:45:15,337
‪when I heard one of our artists
‪got into trouble again.

493
00:45:15,421 --> 00:45:17,840
‪I was late because we had
‪an emergency meeting about it.

494
00:45:20,342 --> 00:45:22,136
‪I thought your trouble ended with me.

495
00:45:22,219 --> 00:45:24,680
‪I guess there's another troublemaker.

496
00:45:24,763 --> 00:45:26,932
‪Compared to the trouble you got into,

497
00:45:27,015 --> 00:45:29,017
‪this is peanuts.

498
00:45:29,101 --> 00:45:32,229
‪You're a legendary troublemaker.

499
00:45:39,319 --> 00:45:42,406
‪So, Reporter Joo Jae-geun
‪from Donggwang Daily

500
00:45:43,115 --> 00:45:45,576
‪has been begging to meet you,

501
00:45:45,659 --> 00:45:47,202
‪but I managed to put a stop to it.

502
00:45:48,203 --> 00:45:50,414
‪I'll give you his number later.

503
00:45:50,914 --> 00:45:52,332
‪If he calls, don't answer.

504
00:45:53,500 --> 00:45:54,835
‪Same goes for Reporter Han Su-jin.

505
00:45:54,918 --> 00:45:58,130
‪She asked if you were performing today,

506
00:45:58,797 --> 00:46:00,382
‪but I told her no.

507
00:46:01,091 --> 00:46:01,925
‪Okay.

508
00:46:02,593 --> 00:46:03,427
‪Thanks.

509
00:46:04,094 --> 00:46:06,388
‪Where are you performing today?

510
00:46:09,725 --> 00:46:10,726
‪Today?

511
00:46:21,069 --> 00:46:23,030
‪REGIONAL EMERGENCY MEDICAL CENTER

512
00:47:02,986 --> 00:47:04,613
‪Excuse me. Mr. Kang?

513
00:47:06,406 --> 00:47:08,575
‪I really enjoyed your performance.

514
00:47:09,326 --> 00:47:10,994
‪I don't know much about classical music,

515
00:47:11,078 --> 00:47:13,664
‪but what you have
‪feels like a divine blessing

516
00:47:13,747 --> 00:47:15,207
‪because it strikes a chord.

517
00:47:15,832 --> 00:47:16,667
‪Thank you.

518
00:47:17,709 --> 00:47:19,169
‪By the way,

519
00:47:20,003 --> 00:47:23,131
‪do you know
‪how Conductor Choi Jeong-yo is doing?

520
00:47:25,050 --> 00:47:26,093
‪No.

521
00:47:26,176 --> 00:47:28,053
‪Oh, I see.

522
00:47:29,638 --> 00:47:33,559
‪I was just asking
‪because I was worried about his health.

523
00:47:35,018 --> 00:47:35,894
‪If you'll excuse me.

524
00:47:36,728 --> 00:47:39,022
‪Wait. What do you mean by that?

525
00:47:39,898 --> 00:47:41,525
‪Is Jeong-yo sick?

526
00:47:42,150 --> 00:47:43,277
‪Oh…

527
00:47:43,360 --> 00:47:46,405
‪I've actually been looking for Jeong-yo
‪ever since he disappeared.

528
00:47:47,322 --> 00:47:51,076
‪Please tell me whatever you know.

529
00:47:51,952 --> 00:47:54,538
‪I shouldn't have said anything.

530
00:47:54,621 --> 00:47:56,623
‪I can't share patient information.

531
00:47:58,417 --> 00:47:59,501
‪Please, sir.

532
00:48:00,043 --> 00:48:02,713
‪I really want to find Jeong-yo.

533
00:48:10,262 --> 00:48:12,055
‪Conductor Choi Jeong-yo

534
00:48:12,681 --> 00:48:15,601
‪was one of my patients who used to
‪come in for treatment regularly.

535
00:48:16,393 --> 00:48:19,062
‪A gunshot wound to the shoulder years ago

536
00:48:19,146 --> 00:48:21,898
‪left him with a brachial plexus injury,

537
00:48:22,399 --> 00:48:25,777
‪and it was causing his hand
‪to slowly lose motor function.

538
00:48:28,614 --> 00:48:31,408
<i>‪He suddenly said</i>
<i>‪there was something he had to do</i>

539
00:48:31,491 --> 00:48:33,076
<i>‪and asked for an injection.</i>

540
00:48:33,785 --> 00:48:36,622
<i>‪I told him he might</i>
<i>‪permanently lose the use of his hand</i>

541
00:48:37,205 --> 00:48:40,000
<i>‪if he was overtreated like that.</i>

542
00:48:40,917 --> 00:48:42,586
<i>‪But I couldn't talk him out of it.</i>

543
00:48:44,046 --> 00:48:45,756
‪So I gave him the injection.

544
00:48:46,590 --> 00:48:47,799
‪After a while,

545
00:48:48,550 --> 00:48:50,260
‪he stopped coming to see me.

546
00:48:50,344 --> 00:48:52,429
‪Then I heard he had retired,

547
00:48:52,512 --> 00:48:54,348
‪so I felt bad for him as his doctor.

548
00:48:54,848 --> 00:48:55,849
‪That's why

549
00:48:56,391 --> 00:48:59,144
‪I thought to ask you about him.

550
00:49:04,483 --> 00:49:05,692
<i>‪Nine years ago,</i>

551
00:49:06,610 --> 00:49:08,737
‪I got shot in my right shoulder.

552
00:49:09,738 --> 00:49:11,323
‪It caused nerve damage in my fingers.

553
00:49:11,406 --> 00:49:14,201
‪I can get through daily life,
‪but I can't play anymore.

554
00:49:16,828 --> 00:49:17,954
<i>‪What's going on?</i>

555
00:49:18,038 --> 00:49:20,457
‪Why? You surprised?

556
00:49:21,249 --> 00:49:24,419
‪I kept up with my hospital treatments
‪just in case.

557
00:49:24,503 --> 00:49:27,422
‪Then somehow, my fingers started working.

558
00:49:29,299 --> 00:49:30,342
‪Well?

559
00:49:30,425 --> 00:49:31,635
‪Was it any good?

560
00:49:47,192 --> 00:49:49,236
‪CHOI JEONG-YO

561
00:51:44,935 --> 00:51:47,020
‪HE'S USING HIS WRISTS DIFFERENTLY,
‪BUT I STILL THINK IT'S HIM.

562
00:52:00,534 --> 00:52:01,785
‪ANOTHER NEMESIS MASTER BESIDES KANG?

563
00:52:01,868 --> 00:52:04,204
‪I THINK IT'S KANG PI-O, PLEASE COME BACK

564
00:52:43,326 --> 00:52:45,495
‪TRY A MORE RELAXED RUBATO IN THE LEFT HAND
‪FOR THE 2ND MOVEMENT.

565
00:52:45,579 --> 00:52:47,414
‪AND STRIP OUT THE ORNAMENTS
‪IN THE MIDDLE SECTION.

566
00:52:52,878 --> 00:52:54,129
‪CZECH REPUBLIC

567
00:53:10,353 --> 00:53:12,022
‪CHURCHES IN THE CZECH REPUBLIC

568
00:54:07,744 --> 00:54:09,371
‪Why are you going there?

569
00:54:09,454 --> 00:54:11,706
‪It's not a tourist place.

570
00:54:11,790 --> 00:54:14,417
‪You can't even drive a car there.

571
00:54:15,335 --> 00:54:16,962
‪I'm here to see a friend.

572
00:54:17,879 --> 00:54:19,881
‪Oh, I see.

573
00:56:01,107 --> 00:56:02,484
‪Good job, everyone.

574
00:56:02,567 --> 00:56:06,196
‪With a little more practice,
‪we'll be good enough to perform on stage.

575
00:56:06,905 --> 00:56:10,575
‪Let's have the altos take a break
‪while the sopranos…

576
00:57:49,757 --> 00:57:51,718
‪FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

577
00:57:53,219 --> 00:57:55,138
<i>‪You really don't remember me?</i>

578
00:57:55,221 --> 00:57:57,849
‪You lent me your handkerchief
‪when I asked.

579
00:57:58,600 --> 00:57:59,851
‪And we played four hands.

580
01:00:57,445 --> 01:00:58,279
<i>‪-Play freely…</i>
<i>‪-Play freely…</i>

581
01:00:59,238 --> 01:01:00,198
<i>‪-like that day.</i>
<i>‪-like that day.</i>

582
01:01:08,414 --> 01:01:13,419
‪Subtitle translation by: Jenny Kim
